      "source_lines": "4-14; 17-34",
      "source_assessment": "Each make-tree invocation creates a fresh mutable two-element block with evaluated none values before testing depth. Internal nodes recursively create both children; check-tree traverses the resulting graph. The stretch reference is released, the long-lived root remains referenced across every temporary-tree depth and iteration, and its final check is executed.",
      "bounded_assessment": "Four bounded output contracts passed for the corrected main. At N4, the actual long-root graph had 127 distinct nodes (64 leaves, 63 internal) and 8,001 pairwise identity comparisons before and after churn. Two additional leaves were distinct and mutation-isolated; the same root survived observed recycle-counter growth from 2 to 46. One diagnostic root alias was retained; no per-tree frees or full-size lifecycle trace is inferred.",
      "bounded_contracts": 4,
      "full_size_work_observed": false
    },
